      "letterGrade": true,
      "note": "Twelve courses of 3 or 4 credits each, totaling at least 42 credits. Identify six of these courses as the advisor-approved concentration, spanning at least two disciplines; record the area and course membership in course notes. The catalog describes approval both in the penultimate semester and during senior year. At most six courses may come from any one discipline; AMST subject codes do not identify disciplines, so verify this with the advisor. Three courses must substantially focus on pre-1900 material and two must address American diversity (social justice or inequality emphasizing race, class, gender and/or sexuality). These requirements and the concentration may overlap each other and the seminar. The page supplies no qualifying course lists, so verify content and that the 4000-level course is a seminar manually. AMST 4998 cannot fill the seminar row. Non-AMST rows require confirmation of an American Studies cross-listing or DUS approval; up to two relevant courses without an AMST cross-listing may count with DUS approval. Cross-listed courses entered under another subject may need their AMST code to avoid the two-course exception limit. The app checks the 3-credit minimum but cannot enforce the 4-credit maximum per course.",
