  "footnote": "Major courses require a letter grade of C or better. Submit the American Studies Major Application to declare; meeting the DUS or undergraduate coordinator about an affiliated advisor is recommended. With DUS approval, study abroad may contribute up to two courses for one semester or three for a full year; verify these limits manually. Concentration examples are visual studies, cultural studies, race and ethnicity, legal and Constitutional studies, American institutions, class and social structure, the American environment, American capitalism, and community-engaged learning and research; these are examples, not fixed tracks. Optional honors requires a B+ average in courses pertinent to the major and a prior research-paper course, a topic and faculty supervisor with application by May 1 of junior year, AMST 4993 then AMST 4994 with satisfactory progress review, a first reader, a roughly 50-60 page thesis by mid-April and an oral exam before finals. Honors is awarded by the advisor and affiliated reader; beginning with 2026-27 graduates, Latin Honors is awarded by the college."
